{
  "id": "spring-rest-handling-uri-parameters",
  "slug": "handling-uri-parameters",
  "title": "Handling Uri Parameters",
  "category": "Spring Framework",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "uri-parameters-in-spring-boot-rest",
      "heading": "URI Parameters in Spring Boot REST",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In REST APIs, clients often pass data through the request URI. These data elements fall into three categories:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            "Query Parameters",
            "Path Variables",
            "Matrix Variables"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Each category offers different mechanisms for conveying data, suited for various use cases."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 37,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "query-parameters",
      "heading": "Query Parameters",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "definition",
          "heading": "Definition:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Query parameters are key-value pairs appended to the end of a URI after a ? symbol. They are commonly used for filtering, sorting, pagination, and passing non-sensitive data."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 28,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "uri-structure",
          "heading": "URI Structure:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "https://api.example.com/products?category=electronics&price=100",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "breakdown",
          "heading": "Breakdown:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "/products: API endpoint",
                "?category=electronics: Query parameter (category)",
                "&price=100: Another query parameter (price)"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 12,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "using-requestparam-in-spring",
          "heading": "Using @RequestParam in Spring:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@GetMapping(\"/products\")\npublic List<Product> getProducts(@RequestParam String category,\n                                 @RequestParam Optional<Integer> price) {\n    // Process based on category and optionally price\n}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "key-points",
          "heading": "Key Points:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "@RequestParam maps query parameters to method arguments.",
                "Use Optional to indicate optional parameters.",
                "Useful for dynamic data like filters."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 19,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "path-variables",
      "heading": "Path Variables",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "definition",
          "heading": "Definition:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Path variables are parts of the URI path, specified using curly braces {}. They are used for identifying specific resources like users or products."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 24,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "uri-structure",
          "heading": "URI Structure:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "https://api.example.com/customers/123",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "breakdown",
          "heading": "Breakdown:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "/customers: Base path",
                "123: Value of the customerId path variable"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 10,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "using-pathvariable-in-spring",
          "heading": "Using @PathVariable in Spring:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@GetMapping(\"/users/{userId}\")\npublic User getUser(@PathVariable Long userId) {\n    // Fetch user by ID\n}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "steps-to-use-path-variables",
          "heading": "Steps to Use Path Variables:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": true,
              "items": [
                "Identify the dynamic segment in the URI (/users/{userId}).",
                "Create a controller method with the path pattern.",
                "Use @PathVariable to bind the URI value to a method argument."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 27,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "key-points",
          "heading": "Key Points:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Compatible with all HTTP methods (GET, POST, DELETE, etc.).",
                "Supports multiple variables: @GetMapping(\"/orders/{userId}/{orderId}\")\npublic Order getOrder(@PathVariable Long userId, @PathVariable Long orderId) { ... }"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 24,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "matrix-variables",
      "heading": "Matrix Variables",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "definition",
          "heading": "Definition:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Matrix variables are embedded within the path segment and separated by semicolons ;. They are useful for adding context-specific filters to individual path segments."
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 24,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "uri-structure",
          "heading": "URI Structure:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "https://api.example.com/customers/123;region=US;age=30",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "breakdown",
          "heading": "Breakdown:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "/customers/123: Path with path variable 123",
                ";region=US: Matrix variable region",
                ";age=30: Matrix variable age"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 14,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "using-matrixvariable-in-spring",
          "heading": "Using @MatrixVariable in Spring:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@RestController\npublic class PlanController {\n\n    @GetMapping(\"/plans/{planId}\")\n    public Plan getPlan(@PathVariable Long planId,\n                        @MatrixVariable(pathVar = \"planId\") List<Integer> localRates) {\n        // Retrieve plan details using matrix variable\n    }\n}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "important",
          "heading": "Important:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "To enable matrix variable support:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Disable removeSemicolonContent in UrlPathHelper:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@Configuration\npublic class WebConfig implements WebMvcConfigurer {\n    @Override\n    public void configurePathMatch(PathMatchConfigurer configurer) {\n        UrlPathHelper pathHelper = new UrlPathHelper();\n        pathHelper.setRemoveSemicolonContent(false);\n        configurer.setUrlPathHelper(pathHelper);\n    }\n}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 9,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "key-points",
          "heading": "Key Points:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Useful when applying multiple filters to a single path segment.",
                "Rarely used compared to query/path parameters.",
                "Requires additional configuration."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 19,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "summary",
      "heading": "Summary",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Format Example",
            "Annotation",
            "Use Case"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Query Param",
              "/products?category=phones&price=1000",
              "@RequestParam",
              "Filters, sorts, optional data"
            ],
            [
              "Path Variable",
              "/users/42",
              "@PathVariable",
              "Identifying specific resources"
            ],
            [
              "Matrix Variable",
              "/plans/42;region=US;type=monthly",
              "@MatrixVariable",
              "Contextual filtering per path segment"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 30,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "best-practices",
      "heading": "Best Practices",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Use query parameters for filtering, sorting, searching.",
            "Use path variables for resource identification.",
            "Use matrix variables sparingly and only if needed.",
            "Always validate and sanitize input parameters.",
            "Use Optional<T> for optional query parameters.",
            "Enable matrix variables explicitly when using them."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 40,
      "subsections": []
    }
